 "in_use_summary_en": "No public sign was found that chest X-rays are reported while the patient waits, or that CT is triggered from radiology, in West Uusimaa or HUS. The HUS pathway describes a referral from the GP to the HUS lung clinic.",
 "missing_en": "",
 "summary_en": "West Uusimaa's imaging page says chest X-rays are taken without an appointment in HUS imaging units, and the HUS lung cancer pathway says the GP refers suspected cases to the HUS lung clinic. Neither page mentions reporting the X-ray while the patient waits or radiology arranging CT directly. A 2023 randomised trial in London (published in Thorax) cut the median time from X-ray to diagnosis from 63 to 32 days.",
